---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import RawShader from "../../components/RawShader.astro";

// The site's greys, with the warm and teal accents of its ASCII banner.
const theme = {
  name: "jacques-mono",
  type: "dark",
  colors: { "editor.background": "#0c0c0c", "editor.foreground": "#d6d4cf" },
  tokenColors: [
    { settings: { foreground: "#d6d4cf" } },
    { scope: ["comment", "punctuation.definition.comment"], settings: { foreground: "#5e5e5e", fontStyle: "italic" } },
    { scope: ["keyword", "storage", "storage.type", "keyword.control"], settings: { foreground: "#ffffff" } },
    { scope: ["string", "string.quoted", "punctuation.definition.string"], settings: { foreground: "#6fbfb0" } },
    { scope: ["constant.numeric", "constant.language"], settings: { foreground: "#e0914f" } },
    { scope: ["entity.name.function", "support.function", "meta.function-call entity.name.function"], settings: { foreground: "#ffffff" } },
    { scope: ["entity.name.type", "support.class", "entity.name.class", "variable.other.constant"], settings: { foreground: "#e0914f" } },
    { scope: ["meta.object-literal.key", "support.type.property-name", "variable.other.property"], settings: { foreground: "#a8a6a1" } },
    { scope: ["punctuation", "meta.brace", "keyword.operator"], settings: { foreground: "#7a7a7a" } },
  ],
};

const models = [
  { name: "d1-omni-600M", href: "https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-omni-600M", weights: "q8 · 405 MB", speed: "34 ms", parity: "63 / 63" },
  { name: "d1-3B", href: "https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-3B", weights: "q4 · 1.5 GB", speed: "166 ms", parity: "55 / 63" },
  { name: "d3-lite", href: "https://huggingface.co/vllm-sr/d3-lite", weights: "q8 · 803 MB", speed: "95 ms · 58 shared", parity: "56 / 56" },
  { name: "Laya", href: "https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya", weights: "q8 · 447 MB", speed: "39 ms", parity: "46 / 48" },
];

const code = `import { Decision } from "./decision.js";

const d3 = await Decision.load("https://huggingface.co/Jacqkues/d3-lite-decisionjs/resolve/main/");
const { answers } = await d3.systemOne(ticket, {
  topic:   { type: "choice", instructions: "What is the topic?",
             criteria: { billing: "billing, payment", delivery: "delivery", bug: "technical bug" } },
  churn:   { type: "noul",   instructions: "Is the customer at risk of leaving?" },
  urgency: { type: "score",  instructions: "How urgent is it?", criteria: ["low", "medium", "high"] },
});
// answers.topic   → { choice: "delivery", confidence: 0.96, probabilities: { … } }
// answers.churn   → { noul: 0.83 }                     P(yes)
// answers.urgency → { score: 1.16, legend: { 0: "low", 1: "medium", 2: "high" } }`;
---
<Base title="decision.js — Jacques" description="decision.js: small decision models (d1, d3-lite, Laya) running in the browser on WebGPU. Typed decisions over any text or JSON, in one forward pass, with no server." fullBleed>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <RawShader scene={9} />
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">WebGPU inference engine — TypeScript</p>
        <h1>decision.js</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Small decision models in the browser, on WebGPU. You give it a state (a support ticket, a form, a log
          line, any JSON) and typed questions; it answers with calibrated probabilities in one forward pass,
          with no token generated and nothing sent to a server.
        </p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/decision/playground">View playground →</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://huggingface.co/Jacqkues/d3-lite-decisionjs">d3-lite weights on Hugging Face</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="page">
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>vs LiteRT.js (ML Drift)</dt><dd>2.1× faster</dd></div>
        <div><dt>d1-omni, per ticket</dt><dd>34 ms</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Same answer as PyTorch</dt><dd>98.9–99.4%</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Dependencies</dt><dd>1 tokenizer</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <article class="prose">
        <h2>The idea</h2>
        <p>
          Decision models like LiquidAI's <strong>d1</strong> or vLLM Semantic Router's <strong>d3-lite</strong> do not chat:
          they read a state and score the options of a question (yes / no, one of N, a level on a scale). That is one
          forward pass and a softmax, so a sub-billion-parameter model is enough, and a laptop GPU can run hundreds of
          decisions per second. decision.js runs them in the page: the data never leaves the browser.
        </p>
        <p>
          The API mirrors the models' own Python API (<code>system_one</code>, <code>probabilities</code>): the same question
          schema, the same prompts token for token, and the same answers.
        </p>
        <Code code={code} lang="ts" theme={theme} />

        <h2>Models</h2>
        <p>
          300 support tickets with 3 questions each (a 7-way choice, a yes/no and a 3-level score), Apple M5 Pro,
          Chrome, matrix units. Parity: same answer as the original model on a deliberately hard set (empty,
          nonsensical and forged states, near-ties).
        </p>
        <div class="table">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Weights</th><th>Per ticket</th><th>Parity</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {models.map((m) => (
                <tr><td><a href={m.href}>{m.name}</a></td><td>{m.weights}</td><td>{m.speed}</td><td>{m.parity}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          On a 465-question sample of the <a href="https://github.com/apolinario/decision-index">Decision Index</a>, d3-lite
          scores 77.8% in the browser against 77.6% for its official PyTorch runtime, with the same answer 98.9% of the time.
        </p>

        <h2>Against Google's LiteRT.js</h2>
        <p>
          On the same 900 sequences in the same Chrome, decision.js runs d1-omni at <strong>34 ms per ticket</strong> against{" "}
          <strong>71 ms</strong> for LiteRT.js 2.5.3, whose WebGPU backend is ML Drift. Running d1-omni there at all took a
          rewritten graph split in four, fp16 weights and an fp16-safe RMSNorm; and its static shapes pad a quarter of the work.
        </p>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One command buffer per batch.</strong> Many questions are packed on one token axis with no padding; per-token metadata tells attention and convolution kernels what each token may read.</li>
          <li><strong>Matrix units.</strong> After ML Drift's design, linear weights are converted once to f16 in 8×8 blocks and the matmul loads them straight into subgroup matrices: 92–94% of what WebGPU reaches on the chip with nothing but multiply-accumulates.</li>
          <li><strong>Fused kernels.</strong> d3-lite's Gated DeltaNet layer (conv, norms, gates, the recurrence and the gated norm) is a single kernel; SwiGLU runs in the matmul's epilogue.</li>
          <li><strong>Only what the answer needs.</strong> Logits are computed for the options' tokens only, at the answer slot.</li>
          <li><strong>Shared state, optionally.</strong> <code>shareState</code> reads a request's state once for all its questions: 95 → 58 ms per d3-lite ticket, at the cost of exactness (77.8% → 76.8% on the Decision Index).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Try it</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/decision/playground">playground</a> runs d3-lite on your GPU: edit the state and the questions, compare the
          exact and shared modes, measure the throughput. It needs WebGPU with f16 and subgroups (a recent Chrome or Edge)
          and downloads the weights once.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { position: relative; height: min(86svh, 52rem); min-height: 34rem; }
  .hero-copy {
    position: absolute; z-index: 5; bottom: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    left: 0; right: 0; max-width: 52rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero-copy > * { text-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9); }
  .hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 4.6rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .hero-copy .cta { pointer-events: auto; }
  .page { max-width: 52rem; padding-top: 3rem; }
  .lede { color: #d6d4cf; font-size: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; max-width: 44rem; }

  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .btn { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55); backdrop-filter: blur(4px); }
  .btn {
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--dim);
    transition: color 0.2s, background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .btn:hover { color: var(--bg); background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); }
  .btn.primary { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); }

  .stats {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .prose :global(pre.astro-code) { background: #0c0c0c !important; }
  .stats div { padding: 1.1rem 1rem 1.2rem 0; }
  .stats div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); padding-left: 1rem; }
  dt { font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  dd { margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--ink); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .stats div:nth-child(3) { border-left: 0; padding-left: 0; }
    .stats div:nth-child(n + 3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  }

  .table { overflow-x: auto; }
  .prose table { width: 100%; }
  .prose td:first-child, .prose th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  .prose pre { white-space: pre; }
</style>
